<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Radius of a small circle</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) A spherical water tank at a school in Machakos has radius \({@exd(Rb)@}\,\text{m}\). The water surface is \({@exd(d)@}\,\text{m}\) above the centre of the tank. Find the radius of the water surface, correct to 2 decimal places.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] m [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Take \(R = 6370\,\text{km}\). Find the radius of the parallel of latitude \({@phi@}^\circ\,\mathrm{[[if test="hn"]]N[[else]]S[[/if]]}\), correct to the nearest km.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] km [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The centre of the tank, the centre of the water surface and a point on its edge form a right-angled triangle. The tank's radius \({@exd(Rb)@}\,\text{m}\) is the hypotenuse and \({@exd(d)@}\,\text{m}\) is one side, so</p><p>\[r^2 = {@exd(Rb)@}^2 - {@exd(d)@}^2 = {@exd(Rb^2-d^2)@}, \qquad r = {@dispdp(float(r),3)@} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(100*r+1/2)/100),2)@}\,\text{m}.\]</p><p>(b) In the cross-section through the poles, the radius of the parallel is the side next to the angle of latitude in a right-angled triangle with hypotenuse \(R\). A parallel is a small circle, radius \(R\cos\varphi\), that shrinks to a point at the pole:</p><p>\[r = 6370 \cos {@phi@}^\circ = {@dispdp(float(rp),1)@} \approx {@floor(rp+1/2)@}\,\text{km}.\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
cosd(x) := cos(x*%pi/180);
sind(x) := sin(x*%pi/180);
atand(x) := 180*atan(x)/%pi;
asind(x) := 180*asin(x)/%pi;
two(v) := if v < 10 then sconcat("0", string(v)) else string(v);
hm(m) := block([q], q: mod(m, 1440), sconcat(two(floor(q/60)), ":", two(mod(q, 60))));
dmx(m) := sconcat(string(floor(m/60)), "^\\circ", two(mod(m, 60)), "'");
/* Design: radius of a small circle, with a water tank and parallels of latitude. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), chapter 3, Exercise A questions 6 and 7. */
Rb: rand_with_step(3/2,3,1/2);
d: rand_with_step(1/5,Rb-3/10,1/10);
r: sqrt(Rb^2-d^2);
phi: rand_with_prohib(10,70,[45]);
hem: rand(["N","S"]);
hn: is(hem="N");
rp: 6370*cosd(phi);
/* diagnostics */
dRd: Rb-d; dpl: sqrt(Rb^2+d^2); dnr: Rb^2-d^2;
rs: 6370*sind(phi); rc: 40040*cosd(phi); rr: 6370*cos(phi); rl: 6370*(90-phi)/90;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
