  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Navigation: radius of a small circle</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.7 (a) / Essential 2.3 (a): Find the radius of a small circle of a sphere by Pythagoras, and the radius of a parallel of latitude as R cos(latitude).</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3 (The sphere), Exercise A, questions 6 and 7 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: the radius of a small circle; a school water tank and parallels of latitude, new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
